prompt baton prin recur — read REMEMBER + the 1,024-round itinerary + the six-season double-seat, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, approve own design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop at custody gates.
think Read REMEMBER (git nib 61e0636267; HEAD 9ef061c4f6), the 1,024-round itinerary, and the six-season double-seat. The five most recent commits are the Mycelium Lapse arc (design + r1–r4) and a remember-fold. REMEMBER's own frontier line names the next agent-doable crux plainly: a fresh Mycelium journey — an account-statement voice. That is Lindy-first (a ledger no one can read is a ledger no one can trust; legibility compounds) and crux-first (the hardest still-tractable move: a projection that cannot drift from the verdict it reads), and it needs no custody gate.
think Studied the machinery the voice composes: mycelium/fold.rye (signed facts, supply), mycelium/lapse.rye (the resolved two-phase Ledger — Account{pk·balance·reserved·received}, Pledge{from·to·amount·deadline·state·pos}, balance_of/reserved_of/balances_sum/reserved_sum/pledge_at, and lapse.resolve over a Cord Dag), and lapse_true.rye's app==awk r4 shape. The Ledger's public surface is enough to project one account with no edit to any module.
think Named the journey the Statement (comlink-tendency: clear/warm/safe, grep-clean beside Cord·Knot·Till·Purse·Pledge·Braid·Lapse). Wrote the self-approved design round (active-designing/20260813-091851_…) naming the four-rung arc mirroring the seated shape: r1 crux · r2 travels (Bron) · r3 across a Knot · r4 true to the bytes.
think Implemented r1 (mycelium/statement.rye): a Statement is a pure bounded projection of one account — balance·reserved·received plus a bounded list of made/received pledge lines (counterparty·amount·state). The crux property is reconciliation: reserved == the sum of the account's own still-OPEN outbound pledges' amounts (an open pledge is exactly what reserves coins), asserted inside statement_for so a drifted statement cannot compile a green. statements_conserve proves the projection (not merely the ledger) conserves Σ(balance+reserved)==total_issued.
obs GREEN on the first run across five scenes built the proven way (Cord blocks → lapse.resolve): open (Alice reserves 100 to Bob), posted (reserve returns, Bob holds 100), lapsed (Alice's coins home, her line reads lapsed), a stranger (a true zero statement, present=false), and arrival-independence inherited (two round-2 permutations, one identical statement). The rendered open line reads balance=0 reserved=100 received=100, Bob's fingerprint 55154f42… matching the Lapse fixture's Bob.
obs Additive discipline held: composed cord+fold+lapse+kumara public API only, edited no module, each re-runs GREEN at the witness door. TAME style check clean (statement.rye not flagged), width-check clean. Named all buffers/lists by the ledger's own ceilings (lapse_max_pledges, lapse_max_accounts) — no unbounded walk.
loom witness=mycelium_statement_witness scenes=5 reconcile_checks=every_present_account first_run=green
